<title>USA: LaSalle Re to sell $75 mln preferred shares.</title>
<headline>LaSalle Re to sell $75 mln preferred shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>LaSalle Re Holdings Ltd said Tuesady it will sell $75 million of series A preferred shares, which will pay quarterly cash dividends at an annual rate of 8.75 percent and will be redeemable at the option of the company, on or after March 27, 2007.</p>
<p>The company said it intends to use the net proceeds to repurchase common shares of the company, as part of its enhanced capital management strategy.</p>
<p>LaSalle writes high severity, low frequency reinsurance, primarily property catastrophe reinsurance, on a worldwide basis.</p>
</text>
